LESSONS = [
L("Chapter 1 — Every lifecycle event is a document", "12", "<p>Between the hire (module 2) and the last working day, a career inside a firm is a sequence of EVENTS — the confirmation, the promotion, the transfer, the warning, the grievance, the resignation, the exit — and this module's thesis governs all of them: <b>every lifecycle event is a document.</b> Not because paperwork is a virtue, but because of what these events ARE.</p><p><b>Why documents, here of all places.</b> Three reasons, in ascending weight: <b>the record's integrity</b> — module 1 made the employee master a record written by its owning events (the status set by the separation process, the grade by the promotion letter — never by edits), and this module is where those owning events live: an employee history that reads as a document sequence is a career; one that reads as unexplained field changes is the folder-and-memory system's ghost. <b>Procedural fairness</b> — these events touch livelihoods: the warning that shapes a dismissal case, the promotion that passes someone over, the transfer that uproots — and fairness in employment is substantially PROCEDURAL (the person told, heard, and answered, with the trail to prove it), which means the document is not the bureaucracy around the fairness; it largely IS the fairness, and Nigerian employment practice — like employment practice everywhere — tests exactly this when disputes arrive. <b>The downstream readers</b> — every event this module documents is consumed elsewhere: the promotion re-prices across the payroll boundary, the transfer re-homes custody across three other tracks, the separation revokes access across everything the firm runs — and an undocumented event leaves its consumers unserved, which is how the departed keep their logins and the transferred keep two warehouses' keys.</p><p><b>The event catalogue.</b> The module's map: the MOVEMENT events (promotion, transfer, acting roles — Chapter 2), the VOICE event (the grievance — Chapter 3), the CONDUCT events (the disciplinary process and its hard edge, the integrity case — Chapters 4-5), and the EXIT events (resignation and notice — Chapter 6; the separation machinery — Chapter 7). Each with the same anatomy this academy has taught five tracks: the document raised, the process run, the record written, the joins served — and each carrying the maintenance thread module 1 planted: the spine re-pointed, the status honest, the joins updated, at the event, by the event.</p><p><b>The tone, carried forward.</b> Module 1's custody framing governs hardest here, because this module holds the record's most sensitive layer — the warnings, the investigations, the grievances: data whose mishandling harms people directly, fenced by the permission design (module 8 finalises it), discussed on need, and written throughout in the discipline module 5 taught for the manager's log — as if the person will read it, because in these processes especially, they may, and the file that was written professionally is the file that protects everyone in the room. The module's machinery is heavy because its subject is heavy; the consultant who installs it well has given the firm the thing disputes test and cultures remember: a way of dealing with people that is the same way, every time, on paper.</p>"),
L("Chapter 2 — Promotions, transfers & acting roles: the movement events", "14", "<p>People move — up, across, and temporarily — and each movement is a document with joins to serve. The movement chapter.</p><p><b>The promotion.</b> The event that module 5 built the case for (the folder, the rationale, the panel where scale permits) and module 6 built the readiness for (the rung's certifications held) — executed as a document: the promotion letter (the new designation and grade, the EFFECTIVE DATE that everything downstream reads, the new terms referenced to the grade band — module 2's offer discipline at the internal market), the record's fields written by the event (designation, grade, the reporting line where the rung changes it — never edited loose), and the joins served in sequence: the payroll boundary notified through the standing handoff (the re-pricing is theirs; the effective date is the contract), the SPINE re-pointed where the promotion creates reports (the new supervisor's people moved under them — and their OWN former reports re-pointed to whoever inherits: module 1's spine-maintenance law at its busiest moment), the authority map updated (the rung's new authorities granted per module 6's certification gating; the outgrown ones reviewed — the promoted person who keeps every old permission plus the new is permission sprawl growing a career at a time), and the announcement made (the promotion communicated with its evidence-based why where appropriate — module 5's visible-standard culture compounding).</p><p><b>The transfer: the custody event.</b> The movement the multi-branch trade runs constantly, and the one this academy is uniquely equipped to govern — because a branch transfer is not an address change; it is a CUSTODY event across three other tracks: the warehouse custody handed over (the outgoing custodian's closing count SIGNED before custody changes — Inventory's law, now scheduled by the HR event that knows the date first; the incoming custodian's opening count the same document), the till and session authorities remapped (the closing roster of the old branch exits them; the new branch's admits them per certification — module 6's register consulted, not assumed), the cost-center address moved (Accounts 6's dimension following the person, effective-dated, so the payroll boundary's addressed cost lands on the right branch from day one), the SPINE re-pointed (the new manager, the old reports), and the practical layer (the roster released here, assigned there — module 3's coverage checked on both ends: the transfer that strands the old branch's Saturday is the swap-approval logic at event scale). The transfer document carries the checklist; the checklist has owners; and the day-one-ready discipline of module 2's onboarding applies in miniature — the transferred person arriving to granted access and an expecting manager is the same lesson taught again.</p><p><b>Acting roles: the temporary movement.</b> The gap-cover appointment (the maternity cover of module 4, the vacancy pending module 2's pipeline, the leave-season stretch) — governed lightly but governed: the acting appointment in writing (the scope of the acting authority — WHICH of the role's powers transfer, because the acting branch manager may hold the roster and the till oversight without the disciplinary pen; the END condition — the date or the event that closes it), the allowance question routed to policy and the boundary (acting pay is a policy the firm sets and payroll computes — never a corridor arrangement), the authorities granted temporarily and REVOKED at the end (the acting period that quietly never ends is a promotion nobody approved — the expiry-tracked appointment, module 1's worklist carrying one more date), and the development read taken (the acting period is the richest audition the firm runs — module 6's succession machinery reading its results deliberately).</p>"),
L("Chapter 3 — Grievances: the employee's channel", "13", "<p>The voice event: the employee's formal channel for raising what is wrong — and the machinery that makes raising it safe, answered, and useful. The grievance chapter.</p><p><b>Why the channel must exist.</b> The pressure-valve argument, made to owners who think a grievance procedure invites grievances: the grievances EXIST regardless — the pay dispute, the roster unfairness, the supervisor's conduct, the colleague conflict — and the only question is where they go: into a CHANNEL (raised, heard, answered, recorded) or into the CORRIDOR (festering, recruiting sympathisers, surfacing eventually as attrition, sabotage-adjacent disengagement, or the tribunal claim that opens with <i>I had no one to complain to</i>). The channel is cheaper in every currency — and its mere credible existence resolves half its cases upstream, because the supervisor who knows complaints have somewhere to go supervises differently.</p><p><b>The process.</b> The shape (the adviser confirms the firm's specifics): RAISED (the grievance in writing — the form or the self-service flow; the informal-first norm honoured where appropriate: many matters resolve at the manager's desk, and the formal channel is for what didn't or can't — including anything about the manager themselves, which routes AROUND the spine to HR or the named alternative: the channel that only runs through the person complained about is a wall with a suggestion-box painted on), ACKNOWLEDGED (within the stated days — the grievance that vanishes into silence teaches the corridor was right), INVESTIGATED (proportionately: the facts gathered, the people spoken to, the records consulted — the reads and documents of six modules frequently settling factual disputes in minutes that memory would litigate for weeks), DECIDED and ANSWERED (the outcome and its reasons to the person, in writing — including the honest 'not upheld, and here is why'), and RECORDED (the case file complete, fenced by the custody rules).</p><p><b>The protections.</b> The channel's load-bearing guarantees: CONFIDENTIALITY (the grievance known to those who must know — the complainant who becomes branch gossip was punished for using the channel, whatever the outcome), NO RETALIATION (the guarantee stated, meant, and watched — the complainant's subsequent treatment read deliberately: the roster that worsens, the rating that dips, the coldness that follows are the channel being poisoned, and the firm that permits it has a channel in name only), and TIMELINESS (the stated clock, kept — justice delayed at trading-firm scale is a person coming to work distressed for weeks).</p><p><b>The altitude read.</b> The layer's aggregate honesty, in the pattern of every module: grievances read per period at altitude — the CLUSTER reads (the theme recurring — pay queries clustering means the boundary's communication is failing, not that people are difficult; the branch clustering means that branch has a management question; the roster-fairness cluster means module 3's rotation rule needs its audit), the VOLUME read with its honest interpretation (zero grievances in a sizeable firm is not harmony; it is more often a channel nobody trusts — the silence read as a flag, not a trophy), and the RESOLUTION read (time-to-answer, upheld rates, the outcomes' follow-through). The grievance layer read this way is a management information system wearing a complaints box — the firm's own people telling it where the machinery grinds, for free, in writing.</p>"),
L("Chapter 4 — The disciplinary process: conduct, governed", "14", "<p>The conduct events — where module 5's capability/conduct fork sends its second branch — and the machinery whose fairness is tested harder than any other in the track. The disciplinary chapter, at consultant altitude with the adviser's boundary bright throughout.</p><p><b>The procedural spine.</b> The shape fairness takes (the firm's specific procedure is the adviser's drafting; the consultant installs and enforces its machinery): the ALLEGATION in writing (the person told exactly what conduct is alleged — specific incident, date, rule engaged: the vague charge is unanswerable and therefore unfair), the person HEARD (the response invited before any decision — in the meeting whose notice gave time to prepare, with the accompaniment norms the firm's procedure provides), the decision by someone IMPARTIAL (not the accuser judging their own accusation — the small firm's honest version: the manager raises, the founder or HR decides; the separation of roles that every track's two-names law prepared this firm to understand), the sanction PROPORTIONATE (matched to the conduct and the history — the ladder below), the decision in WRITING with reasons, and the APPEAL route stated (the second look by someone above or beside the decider — the safety valve that catches the process's own errors). Every step documented; the file the process's proof.</p><p><b>The warning ladder.</b> The graduated response for conduct short of the summary threshold: the NOTED verbal warning (the formal conversation, recorded as held — module 3's documented stage arriving at its destination), the WRITTEN warning (the conduct, the expectation, the timeline, the consequence of recurrence — the document that makes the next step fair), the FINAL written warning (the last rung named as such), and DISMISSAL with notice where the ladder exhausts — with the ladder's disciplines: warnings have SHELF LIVES (the policy's expiry — the five-year-old warning resurrected for today's case is the file weaponised; spent warnings spend), rungs can be SKIPPED only as the procedure provides for graver conduct (the skip justified in writing), and the ladder is climbed for CONDUCT, not capability (module 5's fork, enforced at the gate — the struggling performer on the warning ladder is the confused case both processes fail).</p><p><b>Suspension, governed.</b> The instrument most misused in the wild: suspension is NOT a punishment — it is a neutral holding measure pending investigation (the person whose presence could compromise the inquiry or the workplace stepped aside while facts are gathered), governed accordingly: in writing (the reason, the expected duration, the contact terms), normally on pay (the unpaid 'suspension' that is really a sanction-before-hearing is the procedure inverted — the adviser's terrain, and the firm's exposure), time-bounded (the suspension that drifts for months is a constructive verdict nobody signed), and CLOSED formally (the return with the matter resolved, or the process's next step — never the limbo that punishes by uncertainty). Module 4's boundary line completes here: suspension is not leave, appears in no leave ledger, and carries its own attendance category — the taxonomies kept honest on both sides.</p><p><b>The evidence base.</b> The quiet advantage a structured firm brings to every conduct case: the FACTS are usually already recorded — the attendance marks against the published roster (module 3), the session records, the receiving trails, the regularisation history, the manager's log, the training record answering was-the-rule-communicated (module 2's acknowledgments; module 6's completions) — so the disciplinary process in this firm argues about MEANING, rarely about facts, which shortens every case and protects every party: the person facing records can answer records; the person facing recollections is fighting fog. The chapter's closing conviction, for the consultant to carry into every installation: <b>the disciplinary machinery is not built for the guilty; it is built for the innocent</b> — the wrongly accused person's best friend is a process that demands specifics, hears them, decides impartially, and writes everything down.</p>"),
L("Chapter 5 — Integrity cases: the trade's hard edge", "14", "<p>The gravest conduct cases — theft, fraud, falsification — where the trade's realities, four tracks of controls, and the law converge. The hard chapter, handled with the care it demands.</p><p><b>Where these cases come from.</b> In a structured firm, integrity cases rarely arrive as anonymous tips — they arrive as READS: the session variance pattern (Accounts 3's till data — the operator whose shortages cluster on their shifts), the count discrepancy that localises (Inventory 4's variance taxonomy pointing at a location, a shift, a hand), the seal broken between checkpoints (Inventory 6's forensics), the proxy check-in surfaced (module 3's orphan reads), the unexplained adjustment authored (the two-names log), the never-on-leave tell (module 4's mandatory-leave conviction closing its loop). The controls were built to prevent and detect; when they detect, this chapter governs what happens next — and the first discipline is the reads' own epistemics: <b>a pattern is a question, not a verdict</b> (module 3's law, at its heaviest application) — the variance cluster has innocent explanations (the shift's traffic, the float process, the training gap) that the investigation must genuinely test, because the integrity case that starts as a conclusion ends as an injustice or a tribunal loss, and usually both.</p><p><b>The investigation discipline.</b> Facts before accusations, mechanised: the evidence PRESERVED first (the records exported and secured, the documents copied, the till or stock frozen for counting where the case needs it — the money tracks' freeze discipline serving its gravest customer), the scope defined (what period, what records, what question), the facts assembled from the machinery (the structured firm's advantage again — the timeline built from records, not recollections), the person's ACCOUNT taken properly (within the disciplinary procedure's protections — heard, on notice, accompanied per the procedure; their explanation genuinely weighed, because it is sometimes right), corroboration sought where accounts conflict, and the file built to the standard its consumers demand — the disciplinary decision, possibly the criminal process, possibly the tribunal: three audiences, one file, written once, professionally.</p><p><b>The boundaries, bright.</b> The lines the consultant never crosses and teaches the firm not to: the CRIMINAL boundary (theft and fraud are crimes; the decision to involve the police is the firm's, taken with the adviser — and the internal process and any criminal process are DISTINCT tracks with distinct standards: the firm's disciplinary decision runs on its own procedure and evidence, and neither waits for nor substitutes the other; the adviser choreographs where both run), the RECOVERY boundary (restitution and its instruments — the guarantor framework of module 2 finally cashing its purpose — are the adviser's drafting; the improvised salary-deduction 'agreement' extracted in the heat of discovery is exposure wearing efficiency), and the CUSTODY boundary at its most acute (the case file's confidentiality absolute — the accused person's name in branch circulation before any finding is a wrong the firm cannot un-do, and a liability it authored).</p><p><b>The dismissal done properly — versus the quiet resignation.</b> The chapter's ethical summit: the proven case concluded through the procedure — the dismissal with its documented why — versus the trade's common shortcut: the quiet resignation (the person 'allowed to resign', the matter unrecorded, the reference unremarkable) — and the shortcut's true price named: it EXPORTS the problem (the till-skimmer hired by the pharmacy across town on a clean reference — the trading community's integrity commons, polluted), it forfeits the deterrence (the workforce that watched theft resolve into a tidy exit has been taught the actual odds), and it corrupts the reference layer this track's module 2 depends on (the firm that gives sanitised references receives them — the verification gate everyone's pipeline runs is only as honest as everyone's exits). The honest practice, adviser-shaped: conclude the process, record the truth, and answer reference requests factually within the law's bounds — the firm's contribution to the commons it draws from. The chapter closes where it opened: the controls' purpose was never prosecution — four tracks said 'protect the honest' at every layer, and the integrity process run properly is that promise kept at its hardest moment: the honest majority watching learns the machinery is real, fair, and on their side.</p>"),
L("Chapter 6 — Resignation & notice: the voluntary exit", "13", "<p>Most exits are chosen — the resignation — and the firm's handling of its notice period is a discipline with compounding returns. The voluntary-exit chapter.</p><p><b>The resignation as document.</b> The letter received and ACKNOWLEDGED in writing (the acceptance stating the notice terms as the contract sets them, the last working day computed and confirmed — the date every downstream process will read; the ambiguity that surfaces at full-and-final was born here if it was born at all), the notice period per the contract and grade (the terms module 2's offer set, now cashing), and the record's status machinery engaged (the notice-period state — module 1's taxonomy — with the separation checklist of Chapter 7 OPENED the same day, because the checklist's longest lines start immediately).</p><p><b>The notice period, managed.</b> The weeks between letter and last day, run deliberately: the HANDOVER begins day one (the academy's handover test — every track's module 8 — now run live and compressed: the documents current?, the deputy ready?, the successor named or the acting appointment drafted? — the notice period is the handover test with a deadline, and the firm that built module 6's succession machinery discovers its notice periods are calm while its competitors' are scrambles), the leave-during-notice rules applied as module 4 set them (the balance's fate resolved by policy toward the final settlement — not negotiated at the door), the duties honest (the notice-period employee doing real work, not ghosted at their desk nor loaded with the backlog as a parting gift — both patterns read by everyone watching), and the security judgment made where the role demands it (the departing employee in a sensitive seat — the finance roles, the systems administrator — may serve notice away from the controls per the firm's policy and the adviser's shape: garden-leave logic at trade scale, applied by risk, not routine).</p><p><b>The counter-offer question.</b> Handled honestly, because every owner asks: the counter-offer that addresses a REAL and fixable cause (the pay genuinely under band — the grade conversation that should have happened at module 5's cycle happening late) sometimes holds; the counter-offer that outbids a decided departure usually buys months, not years (the decided leaver re-resigns on schedule, now with a raise), and the systematic counter-offer culture teaches the workforce that resignation is the negotiation channel — the corridor's politics given a formal doorway. The consultant's framing: the counter-offer is a symptom conversation — WHY the resignation, answered honestly, is worth more than the retention, and Chapter's exit interview is where the answer gets recorded even when the person still leaves.</p><p><b>The signals read.</b> The resignation layer at altitude, closing the chapter: the pre-resignation drift (module 3's attendance decay named exactly this — the signal that wanted a check-in months ago: each resignation audited briefly against its warning signs, not for blame but for the detector's tuning), the CLUSTER reads (the manager whose team resigns in series is a management finding — the exit data of Chapter 7's interviews aggregating into the read; the role that churns is module 2's mis-scoped role finding; the post-change wave is the change's bill), and the tenure read (the firm losing its people at year two has an entry problem or a ladder problem — module 6's rungs answering). Attrition read this way is the workforce's referendum, published in resignations — expensive to ignore, free to read.</p>"),
L("Chapter 7 — The separation checklist: the join map reversed", "14", "<p>The exit's machinery — and the chapter where module 1's deepest promise (<i>HR knows about departures before every other control does</i>) is delivered as a checklist. The clean-exit chapter.</p><p><b>The checklist as the join map reversed.</b> Module 1 built the joins — the employee linked to users, tills, warehouses, approvals, mandates; this chapter walks them BACKWARDS: the separation checklist enumerates every link the person holds and resolves each before Left is final. The access layer: the USER account (disabled on the last day — not the following month: the departed with live logins is the security failure every audit finds first), the till and session authorities (the closing roster exits them — module 3's roster adjusted the same week), the warehouse permissions and restrictions (Inventory's fences dismantled), the APPROVER roles (every two-names pattern the person held re-named — the write-off signatures, the payment-run seat, the journal pen: Accounts 3's mandate-review discipline fired by the HR event, exactly as module 1 promised — including the BANK mandates themselves, the same-week signatory removal the money track demanded, now scheduled by the checklist that knew the date first), and the system roles beyond (the report subscriptions, the shared credentials rotated where any existed — the rotation being also the audit that finds them).</p><p><b>The custody layer.</b> The physical and accountable holdings: the warehouse or till CUSTODY handed over with its closing count SIGNED (Inventory's custody law — the count before custody changes, run before the last day, because the discrepancy found after departure is a dispute with an empty chair), the ASSETS recovered against the register (the laptop, the phone, the keys, the vehicle — Accounts 7's asset register consulted per person: the register that tracked the holding now proves the return), the documents and materials in the person's keeping retrieved, and the guarantor file's status noted where the trade's framework applies (module 2's paperwork, closing its loop at exit).</p><p><b>The settlement inputs: the boundary's last package.</b> The full-and-final computation is the payroll function's (the boundary's final crossing) — and HR's checklist hands it clean inputs: the last working day confirmed, the leave balance from the ledger (module 4's ledger settling the payout or the shortfall — the minus-eight-days conversation module 4 warned about, arriving here if governance leaked), the notice terms' status (served, paid in lieu, or shortfall per contract), the deductions with their DOCUMENTS (the loan balance, the governed recovery — never the improvised deduction Chapter 5 convicted), and the acting or allowance ends dated. The package complete, categorised, final — the attendance close's properties (module 3), applied to a career's last month — and the settlement computed once, from one version, which is how full-and-final stops being a negotiation.</p><p><b>The exit interview & the status's last write.</b> The leaving conversation, held by HR (not the line manager — the honesty depends on it), structured briefly (why leaving, what worked, what didn't, would you return, may we contact), recorded to the aggregate (Chapter 6's reads consuming it — the individual interview is a courtesy; the aggregated interviews are a management information stream), and closed with dignity (the thanks meant, the reference process explained, the door's status honest — module 1's rehire machinery remembering this person accurately either way). Then the record's last write: the status set LEFT by the completed process — the checklist signed off, the date entered, the employee number retired with the person (module 1's law, honoured at the end it was written for) — and the file complete: a career, readable start to finish as documents, which is what this track promised in its first chapter and delivers in its last ordinary one.</p>"),
L("Chapter 8 — Case study: HealthTrade's lifecycle year", "16", "<p>The event machinery, run through a full year. Every chapter clocks in.</p><p><b>The promotion executed (Ch. 2).</b> Module 6's succession cashes in: the Ibadan storekeeper's ops-lead promotion — the folder argued (module 5's records), the rung's certifications held (module 6's register), the letter effective-dated, and the joins served in sequence: payroll notified through the boundary, the spine re-pointed (his former reports to the new senior storekeeper — the deputy developed before the vacancy, exactly as designed), the authority map updated with the old permissions REVIEWED (two warehouse fences dismantled, not inherited), and the announcement carrying its why. The transfer that follows (the new ops lead relocating to head office's distribution unit) runs the custody event in full: the closing count signed at Ibadan on his second-last day, the incoming custodian's opening count the same document, the cost center effective-dated — one person, five systems, zero loose ends.</p><p><b>The channel and the ladder (Ch. 3-4).</b> One grievance through the channel: a Lagos till assistant's roster-fairness complaint (her Saturday share running heavy) — acknowledged in two days, investigated in one (module 3's shift-share read settling the FACT in minutes: she was right — the rotation had drifted after a colleague's accommodation), answered in writing with the fix (the pattern rebalanced, the accommodation re-priced into the rotation as module 3's rule always required), and the altitude read noting the theme for the annual rotation audit. One warning ladder engaged: a driver's repeated documentation shortcuts (the tailgate variances of Inventory 6, twice coached through module 5's conversation path, persisting) — the noted verbal, then the written warning with its expectation and timeline; the shortcuts stop; the warning ages toward its shelf life doing exactly what the ladder is for: correcting without ending.</p><p><b>The integrity case (Ch. 5).</b> The hard one, handled properly: month seven's session reads localise a variance pattern — one operator, shortages clustering on solo shifts, ₦47,000 across nine weeks. The discipline holds: evidence preserved first (the session records exported, the till counted under freeze), the pattern treated as a question (the innocent explanations genuinely tested — the float process checked, the training record confirmed current, the shift traffic compared), the account taken within the procedure (on notice, heard, accompanied) — and the explanation failing against the records' specificity. The decision impartial (the founder deciding on the branch manager's file), the dismissal documented with its why, the guarantor framework engaged for recovery under the adviser's drafting, the police question decided WITH the adviser (pursued), and the reference stance settled: factual, within the law. The quiet-resignation shortcut is explicitly declined in the file's closing note — <i>we do not export our problems</i> — and the branch's reaction, watched carefully, is the chapter's thesis proven: the honest majority's trust in the tills VISIBLY rises; two operators separately thank the manager for the variance reads that protect their names.</p><p><b>The resignation and the clean exit (Ch. 6-7).</b> The Lagos accountant resigns (a bigger firm, a real ladder-rung the eleven-person structure could not offer — the exit interview records it honestly: <i>would return; leaving for scope, not grievance</i>). The notice period runs the compressed handover test — and passes, because Accounts 8's structural year built the documentation: the close's checklist transfers in two sittings, the deputy-prepared bookkeeper steps up under a written acting appointment with its end condition, and the security judgment is made calmly (the finance seat's notice served with the payment-release authority remapped week one — risk-based, explained, undramatic). The separation checklist walks the join map reversed: user disabled on the last day, the journal pen and release seat re-named, the BANK mandate removed same-week (the letter to the bank dated before the leaving drinks), assets recovered against the register, the leave ledger settling six days into the final package — computed once, from one version, no negotiation. The status writes LEFT by the process; the number retires; the file reads start to finish as documents. The year's note from the MD closes the case: <i>five events, five documents, zero corridors — and the one we dreaded most is the one the branch trusts us more for.</i></p>"),
L("Chapter 9 — Common mistakes & the seventh law", "13", "<p>The lifecycle layer's scar tissue. Symptom → disease → fix.</p><p><b>Pattern 1 — the undocumented movement.</b> Symptom: grades and designations that changed without letters; effective dates nobody can establish; the promotion the payroll boundary learned about from a complaint. Disease: fields edited instead of events run (Ch. 1-2). Fix: the movement documents with effective dates, fields written only by their owning events, the joins served in sequence — and the record's history readable as a career.</p><p><b>Pattern 2 — the transfer that broke custody.</b> Symptom: the discrepancy discovered after the transfer, disputed with an empty chair; two branches' authorities held at once; the cost still landing on the old branch. Disease: the movement run as an address change instead of a custody event (Ch. 2). Fix: the transfer checklist — the signed closing count BEFORE custody changes, authorities remapped by certification, the dimension effective-dated — one person, every system, no loose ends.</p><p><b>Pattern 3 — discipline by explosion.</b> Symptom: nothing said for months, then dismissal-grade fury over the accumulated file; sanctions improvised at the desk; the procedure discovered during the tribunal. Disease: the process absent until it is needed, which is precisely when it cannot be built (Ch. 4). Fix: the procedural spine installed in peacetime — allegation in writing, the person heard, impartial decision, proportionate sanction, appeal — the ladder climbed rung by rung, and the conviction taught: the machinery is built for the innocent.</p><p><b>Pattern 4 — the quiet resignation.</b> Symptom: proven theft resolving into a tidy exit and a clean reference; the same person surfacing at the competitor's till; the workforce recalibrating the odds. Disease: the shortcut that exports the problem and corrupts the reference commons (Ch. 5). Fix: the process concluded, the truth recorded, references factual within the law — and the deterrence and trust dividends collected from the honest majority watching.</p><p><b>Pattern 5 — the departed with live access.</b> Symptom: the ex-employee's login active for months; the bank mandate bearing a name that left in March; the approval workflow routing to an empty desk. Disease: the join map never reversed (Ch. 7) — the exit as an HR formality instead of a cross-system event. Fix: the separation checklist opened the day the letter lands, the access lines dated to the last day, the mandate letters same-week, and the checklist's sign-off gating the Left status — HR knowing first, and acting first.</p><p><b>Pattern 6 — the full-and-final negotiation.</b> Symptom: settlements haggled at the door; leave balances disputed from memory; deductions improvised; the ex-employee and the firm both feeling robbed. Disease: the inputs never governed upstream (Ch. 7) — the ledger absent, the terms ambiguous, the package assembled from recollections. Fix: the ledger-fed, document-backed settlement package — complete, categorised, final — computed once from one version; the negotiation dissolved by machinery, which is this track's whole method at its last application.</p><p><b>The seventh law.</b> The record, the pipeline, the capture, the entitlement, the conversation, the manufacture — and now the events: <b>every lifecycle event is a document — movements with effective dates and served joins, grievances through a channel that answers, discipline through a procedure built for the innocent, integrity cases investigated before concluded and concluded without exporting, exits through the join map reversed, and the record's every field written by the event that owns it.</b> A career in this firm reads start to finish as documents — which is fairness, security, and history in one design. One module remains: the structure that holds the whole people function — settings, the permission fences, the analytics, the calendar, and the handover test that closes the certification.</p>"),
]

